  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 113 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nThe upper trough will become separated from the main upper flow by \nSaturday and will help to form a very weak blocking pattern as an \nupper high builds over the western CONUS. This will only last \nthrough Saturday as the trough dissipates. A series of weak fronts \nwill help to keep highs mostly in the 70s through mid week even as \nthe upper ridge builds slightly. This will be aided by upper flow \nmostly out of the northwest. Some guidance, mainly the NBM, have \nupper highs reaching back into the upper 80s/low 90s by the end of \nthe forecast period, but the overall pattern (north to northwest \nupper flow and weak cold front) would moreso support highs in the \n70s and 80s.",
